# Ludex needs NO environment variables. This file is a placeholder.
#
# There are no runtime env vars, and none are needed at build time either:
#
#   npm run data:art
#
# ...fetches cover art from Steam and Wikipedia, both of which are public and
# keyless. Leave Vercel's environment variables empty.
#
# (An earlier version used RAWG, which required an API key. It was dropped —
# RAWG's API now returns HTTP 522, and Steam provides better-shaped box art
# for free.)
